{"op":"links","model":"m1","links":[{"id":"l1","from":"deposit","to":"int1","rel":"makes"},{"id":"l2","from":"rate","to":"int1","rel":"raises"},{"id":"l3","from":"int1","to":"bal1","rel":"raises","key":true,"hint":"Where does the $700 go once the year ends, if you leave it alone?","reversed":"The interest is added to the balance; the balance after year one does not create year one's interest.","ask":"Why does leaving the interest in the account matter for next year?","rubric":"added interest becomes part of the money that earns interest, so next year's base is larger"},{"id":"l4","from":"bal1","to":"int2","rel":"makes","key":true,"hint":"Next year's 7% is taken of which amount?","reversed":"Year two's interest is earned on the balance, not the other way round.","ask":"Why is year two's interest $49 more than year one's?","rubric":"it is 7% of $10,700 rather than $10,000; the extra $49 is interest on the $700 of earlier interest"},{"id":"l5","from":"rate","to":"int2","rel":"raises"},{"id":"l6","from":"int2","to":"bal2","rel":"raises"},{"id":"l7","from":"bal1","to":"bal2","rel":"becomes"}]}
